WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.720
- Recently, someone asked me
what the most important element

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.440
of a business slide presentation is.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.977
And after thinking about it for a bit,

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:11.420
it was very clear to me that Action titles

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.070
are actually the most important elements.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.700
So, if by now you're not really sure

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.924
what an action title is or how to come up

00:00:17.924 --> 00:00:20.840
with a very, very strong action title...

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.470
Welcome to another video here
on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.520
My name is Heinrich, I'm a
former McKinsey consultant

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.610
and on my channel I
talk a lot about topics

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.240
such as career success and
also consulting skills.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.720
And surely as a consultant,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.030
one thing that you really need to do well

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.670
is to create slide
presentations in PowerPoint

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.130
or any of these other programs.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.190
So in today's video,

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.830
I want to sharpen your understanding

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.880
why action titles are so important

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.680
and also give you some
very, very tangible tips,

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.990
including an exercise to help you

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.590
come up with the best
possible action titles

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.980
that you can write for your slides.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.957
Let's start by looking
into why action titles

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.420
are so important.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.410
And the key point you have to understand

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.940
is that your presentations
should have a storyline.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.030
And it is the action titles
that bring this story to life.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.000
The main idea is that
if you read your titles

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.810
of your presentation from start to end,

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.170
so every single slide,
just read the titles.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.020
The key idea is that by just doing that,

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.727
you will be able to understand
all the key messages

00:01:24.727 --> 00:01:28.230
of the presentation just by
reading these action titles.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.770
So, why is this even necessary?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.040
Why is this important?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.390
Well try to put yourself into the shoes

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.830
of a C-level manager, you are a CEO,

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:38.770
CFO, any other business unit head,

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.070
any other senior guy in an organization.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.620
Likely, especially these
large blue-chip companies

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.130
that often these
consulting firms work for,

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.300
these C-level people, every
single day, every single week,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.130
they will get several big documents,

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.940
50 pages, hundred pages, or even more,

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.930
of other projects that are going on.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.690
Project updates, progress
reports, deliverables like that.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.510
This is far too much to read.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.520
People like this cannot just read

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.330
every single slide of documents like that.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.400
So, what they will expect you to deliver

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.500
is a document where they
can just skim through,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.020
just read the action titles,

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.400
and just by reading the action titles,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.130
be able to understand
all the key messages.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.100
And this is the so-called
horizontal logic,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.310
the storyline of the presentation.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.620
This needs to come to life
via the action titles.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.130
And then the idea is, of course,

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.903
that if they read something
in the action title

00:02:34.903 --> 00:02:36.245
that is really interesting,

00:02:36.245 --> 00:02:38.490
where they want to learn more about,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.160
then they stop and then
they read the page,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.470
they read the full slide.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.250
This then is the vertical logic.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.083
And here, of course,

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.740
you already understand one key thing,

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.660
when writing strong action titles,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.600
and this is that, of
course, an action title

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.440
should summarize the contents of a slide

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.880
in a clear and concise way.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.090
So, this is the intuition,

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.600
but now you might ask yourself,

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.310
what exactly is an action title?

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.680
So, I try to put down here in definition,

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.650
this is coming from
myself, so no fancy source,

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.570
just my best way of putting it in writing.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.210
And I would define an action title

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.813
by being a header of a slide presentation

00:03:14.813 --> 00:03:18.690
that summarizes the content of the slide,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.600
by formulating a complete sentence.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.560
So, if you wanted something
like here the header,

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.397
also here on top of this slide, saying,

00:03:24.397 --> 00:03:26.750
"Action titles help to
create a clear storyline

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.000
within the presentation."

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.230
This would be the action
title of that slide.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.580
This is what you want to try to achieve.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.860
But what do you write in such a title?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.610
What are the contents supposed to be?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.990
And here I think the best
test that you can do,

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.440
is the test of the so-called "So what?"

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.320
The question of the "So what?"

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.220
And I once created a full video,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.170
just about the concept of
asking this question "So what?"

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.560
I will link it somewhere above here,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.410
if you're interested to
learn more about this

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.560
you're free to check it out.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.480
But in a nutshell, the
"So what?" is a question,

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.710
that you as a project lead
might ask to an associate,

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.040
or consultant who prepared the slide,

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.570
or maybe a partner asks to you,

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:07.600
and this person looks at your slide

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.170
and asks him or herself
the question, "So what?"

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.950
Right? So, so what, why is this relevant?

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.400
What is the implication
of what I see here?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.160
Because maybe the information
on the slide is interesting.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.500
It's data. It's nice.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.640
But what does this mean
for the problem at hand,

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.260
for the thing that I need to solve?

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.700
So in putting together the document,

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.970
you should ask yourself,

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.160
what is the "so what?" of the slide,

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.500
if we really struggle to
come up with the "so what?"

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.050
then this often is a sign that this slide

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.550
maybe isn't that important, right?

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.680
If it does not have a clear "so what?"

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.190
maybe it's something that
rather belongs in the appendix,

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.670
but maybe not in the main deck,

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.420
or maybe take it out completely.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.670
But once you know the "so
what?" make sure the "so what?"

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.910
is clearly stated in the action title

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.580
and then of course, when
you're presenting the slide,

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.370
then the "so what?" is also
what you should be communicating

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.310
in your presentation.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.820
Now let's look into a
couple of best practices

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.610
that you should apply whenever
you write an action title.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.310
And here we'll always have an example

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.503
and then an insight that I
want to draw out from that.

00:05:06.503 --> 00:05:08.103
Here the first example is,

00:05:08.103 --> 00:05:13.103
"managing risk is important
for this project success."

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:16.180
And here, my answer is try to
avoid statements like that.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.570
Try to avoid writing general truths

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.250
that are pretty much always correct.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.060
So of course, managing risks
is pretty much always important

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.550
for this project success, right?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.560
So for almost every project
that will be relevant.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.010
So try to avoid writing
things that are obvious,

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:36.270
really draw out more
insightful things than that.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.610
Next, something like,
"all divisions have found

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.400
to not be following best practices."

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.780
What's often dangerous,
is to write action titles

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.403
with really hard absolute statements.

00:05:48.403 --> 00:05:51.550
Always, never, in every case,

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.110
this is like this, or like that.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:57.350
So these are very hard
statements often are traps

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.220
because there are often
some weird edge cases.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.050
Maybe there is this, like very
little division somewhere,

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.120
who does something that
you were not aware of.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.370
Just my personal learning that often,

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.610
and especially for presented,

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.220
maybe there was like one board member

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.240
sitting in the audience will tell you,

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.440
'no, but this is not
correct, this is wrong.'

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.990
Because you know, it's just enough

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.610
to have one example that contradicts this

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:19.800
and then pretty much you're there

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.630
and need to admit that,
yes, your message was wrong.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.150
What you put on the slide was wrong.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.560
It's not the case that this
is true for all divisions.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.487
Next one,

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:33.120
"Company has potential to
significantly improve profit."

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.660
So here my learning from that is,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.810
try to whenever possible, to
quantify the action titles

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.060
include numbers in the action titles.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.210
So if you make a slide
about profit of a company,

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.570
usually you should always be
able to also put a number.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.170
So what is the profit
improvement potential?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.910
What is the potential for the profit

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.340
that you see in the company?

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.450
Next one, "When conducting
data analysis and interviews,

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.970
we learned a lot about the business."

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.570
So this would be an action title,

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.550
which very much focuses on the process.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:04.160
So what you did, you analyzed data,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.160
conducted interviews, you learned a lot.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.210
This is often not so relevant.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.260
People don't really
care to who you talk to,

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.080
what analysis you conducted.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:15.420
What people are interested
in are the results.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.840
This is one of the key
fundamental principles

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.790
of top down communication.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.540
Again, I don't want to go too
deep into this in this video,

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.220
but I will link another video that I did

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:27.230
about top down communication
above here, check it out.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:30.060
Really one of the most
fundamental concepts

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:32.080
for communication as a consultant,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.630
but also in general, in any
professional environment.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:36.777
Last example here,

00:07:36.777 --> 00:07:39.160
"Results indicate significant potential

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.210
to look into further improvement
measures for the business,

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:45.090
with the goal to increase profits by 50%

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.740
until end of this financial
year for the company."

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.060
So, frankly, I don't even
know what exactly this means.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.950
The point that I wanted to make here is,

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.940
write action titles in a concise way.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.410
Don't use more words than necessary.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.460
Yes, usually there will
be a full sentence,

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.150
but don't just write
for the sake of writing.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.117
The rule is that usually in the title,

00:08:06.117 --> 00:08:09.260
you should not have more
than two lines of title.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.840
So two lines are fine, but
not write more than two.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.720
Now let's put your action title
writing abilities to test.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.890
You see here a standard slide,

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.657
it's from a mock-up
presentation, of course,

00:08:20.657 --> 00:08:23.110
not any actual line engagement.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:24.590
But what you see here is a slide

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.470
where the action title is missing.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:29.817
And I want you to come
up with an action title

00:08:29.817 --> 00:08:31.840
and now to help a little bit out,

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.870
here I would just like briefly
explain what you see here.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:37.370
So here you see a sizing
of a growth potential,

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.790
every potential for this company,

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.110
that could choose to enter these markets.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:45.480
So the North America market
or the Asia Pacific market,

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.680
and then you see different
numbers, you see the market size,

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.180
you see how much of the market
is covered by competitors,

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.014
the current market share, and
other considerations like this

00:08:55.014 --> 00:08:57.105
and in the end, also an EBIT potential

00:08:57.105 --> 00:09:00.600
that the company could receive
from entering these markets.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.280
Now, I would encourage you
to maybe even pause the video

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.670
for a moment and think about for yourself,

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:09.500
what would be a strong action
title for such a slide.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.330
If you want, even write it down.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:12.960
So let's look at a couple examples

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.570
of what you could have written.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:18.280
So the first is "Derived
potentials for an expansion."

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:19.930
And again, feel free to always pause

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.360
and think about this for yourself.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.200
Whether you consider

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.480
that this is a strong action title or not.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.160
Because indeed, I would argue,

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:27.880
this is not even an action title,

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.950
this does not even meet the
definition of an action title.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:32.450
This is a title in the style

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.320
that I know many people like to do it,

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.350
but it's just not what I
would recommend you to do.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.580
And this is, for instance,
if you have a page

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:42.225
that describes the risks
of a certain strategy,

00:09:42.225 --> 00:09:45.570
then just writing risks
in the title, right?

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.140
So it's a title, but
it's not an action title

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.930
in the sense that it doesn't summarize

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:54.730
the key message of a
slide in a full sentence.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.710
Next one, "Expansion to new geographies

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.720
creates a positive EBIT potential"

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.610
EBIT, by the way, for the uninitiated,

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.150
stands for earnings
before interest and tax,

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.710
and pretty much is one
metric of profit, right?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.650
So what is the profit, the
profit potential, of the company.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.480
So what do you think
about this action title?

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.634
And here I would argue that
yes, it meets the definition.

00:10:16.634 --> 00:10:19.057
I mean, it is an action title
following the definition,

00:10:19.057 --> 00:10:21.620
but I would argue it's
not the best action title

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.570
you could write,

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.980
because indeed this seems far too generic.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.540
You could be much more tangible,
much more concrete here.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.557
But let's look into a
couple of other examples.

00:10:30.557 --> 00:10:33.280
"Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:36.040
creates a positive EBIT potential."

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:36.910
I mean, yes, I like it.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.990
It's a bit more rich of information

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.640
and not just talking about geographies,

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.330
but are really mentioning the geographies

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.188
you're interested in.

00:10:43.188 --> 00:10:45.910
But here, quantify if possible,

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.930
Just look at these best
practices whenever possible.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.860
Especially whenever you
have numbers available

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.070
at your disposal,

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:54.810
put them in the action
title and quantify it.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:55.643
Next one,

00:10:55.643 --> 00:10:57.470
"Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.980
creates a positive EBIT
potential of 22 Euro million."

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:03.950
So yes, here I would argue, it's fine.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:06.710
It's already a very strong
and solid action title.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.120
Though, here you could argue

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.810
that this is then a little bit too wordy.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:13.180
You could write this in
a bit more concise way.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:16.380
Usually the fewer words
you use the better.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.637
So here one example,

00:11:17.637 --> 00:11:20.010
"Expansion to North American Asia Pacific

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:22.910
with 22 Euro million EBIT potential."

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.110
And I would argue that, yes,

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:26.370
this is a good and solid action title.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:27.568
Here what's also important to understand

00:11:27.568 --> 00:11:29.430
is that you can write these action titles,

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:30.700
you do not need to write them

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:34.620
like you would write, like,
proper full sentences in a book.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.430
It's completely fine to
take out certain words,

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.670
often you take out articles,
any other filler words,

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.640
which are not absolutely necessary

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.160
to understand the key messages.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:45.690
Obviously you would probably not write

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:47.520
something like this as a
full sentence in a book,

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.670
but here is concise action title.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.760
This is absolutely fine.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.320
So hope this makes sense to you.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.140
